17_dlm functional integration case.

Build with make -C tests/17_dlm. Run its run.sh from the case directory,
or use tests/run.sh. The case starts its own XATMI servers and repeats native operations/transactions for NDRX_TEST_DURATATION seconds
(default 10). DLM requires -dlm and Enduro/X EE;
multiple-RM testing uses a local deterministic native XA fixture, without a DB.
Do not run concurrently with other shared-domain suites.

Stress scenarios use NDRX_TEST_DURATATION in whole seconds, defaulting to 10
when unset or empty. Invalid, nonpositive or out-of-range values fail the test.
Each scenario completes its current operation/cycle before stopping and reports
the completed count and elapsed time. Waiting/recovery cases keep their bounded
single-pass sequence. Use NDRX_TEST_DURATATION=1 for a short check or 300 for load.
Native test clients suppress expected-error chatter; servers retain error logs.
Use the existing Enduro/X logging configuration for a short verbose diagnosis.

The build generates protocol field constants with mkfldhdr from the installed
SDK's share/endurox/ubftab/Exfields table, located through pkg-config. Override
EXFIELDTBL when using another matching field table. Generated Exfields.go stays
in the case's src/ubftab package and is not checked in.
